{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "nodeID": "179",
   "text": "How did China choose to respond to tariff pressure, and what does that reveal about managed trade?",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "question",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_jan_31_20#Q"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "180",
   "text": "Industrial policy is non-negotiable; the state can direct commodity purchases",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_jan_31_20#P1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "181",
   "text": "The capacity to deliver purchases is the same capacity that can withdraw them",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "hidden_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_jan_31_20#P2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "182",
   "text": "\"I was surprised by the size of China's impact... I thought U.S. soy would prove to be more of a pure commodity\" — and \"I don't think many expected\" reserves to stay stable",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "revised_prior",
   "toulmin": "revision",
   "oper": "revision",
   "localID": "setser_jan_31_20#P3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "183",
   "text": "\"Chinese data never quite fully lines up, which bothers me more than most\"",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "source_credibility",
   "toulmin": "backing",
   "oper": "backing",
   "localID": "setser_jan_31_20#SC"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "184",
   "text": "Yuan -8% vs USD and -4% vs basket; Treasury holdings flat once Belgian accounts are counted; China is two-thirds of global soybean imports; U.S. beans traded at a discount to Brazil",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_jan_31_20#E1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "185",
   "text": "His own Senate testimony; Toloui on balance-sheet policy; the Economist on managed trade",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_source",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_jan_31_20#E2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "186",
   "text": "Outflow controls and the absence of carry-trade leverage prevented a 2015-style panic",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_jan_31_20#M1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "187",
   "text": "Treasuries carry no leverage — if China pushed yields up, the Fed would simply react",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_jan_31_20#M2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "188",
   "text": "Five parallel verdicts: industrial policy untouched, currency buffered, Treasuries unused, manufactures spared, ag and energy targeted",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_jan_31_20#C1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "189",
   "text": "China can meet its 2020 commitments — and that is precisely the risk. \"What China's state gives, China's state can take away\"",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "main_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_jan_31_20#K"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "190",
   "text": "Both approaches carry costs — managed trade rewards diversion away from allies, while the conventional approach changed little in 2010-11",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "opposing_view",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_jan_31_20#X"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "191",
   "text": "Tech decoupling will not bite in 2020: Boeing's own problems, no indigenous jet engines, semiconductors too early",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_jan_31_20#QF"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "192",
   "text": "Why were manufactures spared? \"I am not quite sure why this is the case\" — two theories offered, neither chosen",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "other_explanation",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_jan_31_20#R1"
  },
